# ARK Website Admin

**Full doc:** [ark-website-admin-v1.md](../../docs/platform/ark-website-admin-v1.md)

## The sentence

**Owners manage their website. Growth explains why it performs and what to improve next.**

Not a fourth application. A **product inside the Admin Platform** alongside Growth, Voice, and Settings.

## Admin Platform (target nav)

```
Website · Growth · Voice · Settings
```

## Two tabs, two questions

| Tab | Owner question | Rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Manage** | What do customers see? | Presentation + publishing |
| **Performance** | How is my website doing? | **Summarize only** — deep-link to Growth |

**Website asks:** *How is my website doing?*  
**Growth asks:** *Why, and what should we improve?*

**Website never explains why.** Website tells the owner what they can manage and how the website is performing. Growth explains why performance changed and what should be improved.

## Authority (do not merge)

| Product | Owns |
| --- | --- |
| **Website** | Presentation, publishing, owner UX |
| **Growth** | Sessions, attribution, opportunities, optimization |
| **Settings** | Shop operations — not the website mental home |

Never move Growth into Website. Never bury website Manage in Shop Settings long-term. **Deep-link, don't duplicate.**

## CMS litmus

Every Manage feature must answer:

> Does this help the shop present itself better or convert more visitors?

WordPress parity is a reject.

## Implementation

- Routes: `/app/website/*` as presentation over existing authority
- Phase 1: nav + Manage (re-home public surface settings) + Performance (projections + Growth links)
- Customer shell unchanged — see [ark-website-doctrine.mdc](ark-website-doctrine.mdc)
